=== plain-80: width 80, height 24, profile notty, dark, glyphs ascii, plain
# logs pager-commands ------------------------------------------$
$
# Note$
# Inferred from v0.3.2 and origin/main. What would run, by the$
# environment: PAGER is not read, kept or dropped (decision 7$
# (a)). Under sudo, sudo-rs and doas it is dropped [I; not run$
# for PAGER]. LESSSECURE=1 turned off !, |, v, E and :e in GNU$
# less 668 on the VMs, as a user, not as root (vm-runs/s1/04-$
# less2-*). On BusyBox's less it changed nothing, s and E still$
# prompting; that they write and open any path as root is read$
# (miscutils/less.c, master): no path was typed at s, and E$
# tried only a name that does not exist. Alpine's less package$
# is [I, not run]. The gallery's table: nothing runs.$
$
# pager-less, adopted ------------------------------------------$
$
   -  root login, PAGER=most$
      less -- /var/log/hardn.log$
   -  sudo, PAGER dropped$
      less -- /var/log/hardn.log$
   -  sudo-rs, PAGER dropped [I]$
      less -- /var/log/hardn.log$
   -  doas, BusyBox's less$
      None: BusyBox's has no secure mode$
   -  doas, the less package [I]$
      less -- /var/log/hardn.log$
   -  sudo, PAGER=most kept$
      less -- /var/log/hardn.log$
   -  no less, no PAGER$
      None: the last lines alone$
$
# Its environment ----------------------------------------------$
$
   -  LESSSECURE           1$
   -  LESSHISTFILE         -$
   -  TERM                 xterm-256color$
   -  LC_ALL               C.UTF-8$
$
$

